* power_supply_datasheet_models.lib
* Datasheet-built SPICE models for power_supply.kicad_sch (simulation only).
* Every value comes from the datasheet of the part JLCPCB will fit (LCSC number given),
* read from its table or its typical-characteristics graph. Tags:
*   [T] typical value or typical curve      [M] only a max (or min) is given, that limit is used
*   [D] not on the datasheet: SPICE default (no effect) or a stated assumption
* Forward curves were fitted to 4-6 points read off the typical graph; fit error is listed.

* =====================================================================
* D1  SS510C, Shandong Jingdao, LCSC C123944 (SS52C-SS520C datasheet, 2017.01)
*   Forward: Fig.3 typical, SS510C curve, fitted 0.1-10 A (error within 7 %)       [T]
*   Leakage: Is 10 uA, from Fig.2 typical reverse current at 25 C (4-10 uA)          [T]
*   Capacitance: Fig.4 typical, SS56C-SS520C curve (610 pF at 0.1 V, 214 pF at 80 V) [T]
*   Breakdown: 100 V = VRRM rating; IR 1 mA max at 100 V                            [M]
*   Schottky: no reverse-recovery charge (TT = 0)                                  [D]
* =====================================================================
.subckt SS510C A K
D1 A K D_SS510C
.model D_SS510C D(Is=1e-5 N=1.095 Rs=0.0743 Ikf=0.0497 Cjo=627p Vj=0.548 M=0.213 Bv=100 Ibv=1m Tt=0)
.ends SS510C

* =====================================================================
* D2, D4  ES1J-LTP, MCC, LCSC C86560 (ES1A-L thru ES1J-L, Rev. E 2015)
*   Forward: Fig.1 typical, ES1J-LT curve, fitted 10 mA-3 A (error within 3 %)     [T]
*   Leakage: Is limited to IR 5 uA max at 600 V                                    [M]
*   Capacitance: Fig.5 typical (34 pF at 0.01 V, 15 pF at 4 V, 4 pF at 100 V)       [T]
*   Recovery: Trr 35 ns max (IF 0.5 A, IR 1 A, Irr 0.25 A) -> Tt = 35n/ln(1.5) = 86 ns [M]
*   Breakdown: 600 V = VRRM rating                                                 [M]
* =====================================================================
.subckt ES1J A K
D1 A K D_ES1J
.model D_ES1J D(Is=5e-6 N=2.94 Rs=0.178 Ikf=0.00632 Cjo=30.7p Vj=1.117 M=0.442 Tt=86n Bv=600 Ibv=5u)
.ends ES1J

* =====================================================================
* D3, D5  SMBJ130A, Littelfuse, LCSC C224006 (SMBJ series, rev. 2025)
*   Breakdown: VBR 144-159 V at 1 mA, no typical -> midpoint 151.5 V                [M]
*   Clamping slope: VC 209 V at IPP 2.9 A -> (209-151.5)/2.9 = 19.8 ohm             [M]
*   Leakage: IR 1 uA max at VR 130 V                                               [M]
*   Capacitance: Fig.5 typical, uni-directional at VBR 151 V: 250 pF at 0 V, 49 pF at VR [T]
*   Forward: Fig.7 typical single die, rough fit (only conducts if a rail reverses) [T]
* =====================================================================
.subckt SMBJ130A A K
Df A K D_SMBJ_F
Dbd A Y D_SMBJ_BD
Rbd Y K 19.8
.model D_SMBJ_F D(Is=1e-13 N=1 Rs=0.05 Cjo=250p Vj=1.051 M=0.338)
.model D_SMBJ_BD D(Is=1e-15 N=1 Bv=151.5 Ibv=1m)
.ends SMBJ130A

* =====================================================================
* D6, D9, D10  BZT52C12, hongjiacheng / R+O, LCSC C19077410 (BZT52C2V0-C75, Rev 2.1)
*   Zener voltage: 12.0 V typ at IZT 5 mA (table, 11.4-12.6 V)                     [T]
*   Dynamic impedance: about 12 ohm at 12 V, Fig.4 typical (ZZT max 25 ohm)         [T]
*   Leakage: IR 0.1 uA max at 8 V                                                  [M]
*   Forward: VF 0.9 V max at 10 mA, no typical curve                               [M]
*   Capacitance: Fig.3 typical at 12 V: 50 pF at 0 V, 40 pF at 1 V                 [T]
* =====================================================================
.subckt BZT52C12 A K
Df A K D_BZT_F
Dz A Y D_BZT_Z
Rz Y K 12
.model D_BZT_F D(Is=1.4e-17 N=1 Rs=1 Cjo=50p Vj=1.208 M=0.371)
.model D_BZT_Z D(Is=1e-16 N=1 Bv=11.94 Ibv=5m)
.ends BZT52C12

* =====================================================================
* D7, D8  BAS21, hongjiacheng / R+O, LCSC C7502725 (BAS21 thru BAS21S, Rev 2.0)
*   Forward: Fig.1 typical 25 C, fitted 10 uA-100 mA (error within 1.5 %)          [T]
*   Capacitance: Fig.3 typical (1.2 pF at 0 V, 0.95 pF at 20 V)                    [T]
*   Breakdown: 250 V at 100 uA (table)                                             [T]
*   Recovery: table gives Trr 5.0 ns max, the feature list says < 50 ns (conflict);
*             5.0 ns used -> Tt = 5n/ln(1+30/30) = 7.2 ns                          [M]
* =====================================================================
.subckt BAS21 A NC K
D1 A K D_BAS21
Rnc NC K 1G
.model D_BAS21 D(Is=2.02e-12 N=1.076 Rs=1.859 Ikf=0.001 Cjo=1.2p Vj=0.05 M=0.039 Bv=250 Ibv=100u Tt=7.2n)
.ends BAS21

* =====================================================================
* Q3, Q4, Q5  MMBTA42, JSCJ (Jiangsu Changjiang), LCSC C8515
*   hFE about 170 flat 0.1-20 mA, 49 at 100 mA (typical curve, VCE 10 V)          [T]
*   VBE 0.62 V at 1 mA, VCE 10 V (typical IC-VBE curve)                            [T]
*   Early voltage about 100 V from the typical IC-VCE curves                       [T]
*   VCE(sat) 85 mV to 160 mV, 1-100 mA, beta 10 (typical curve) -> Rc 0.8 ohm       [T]
*   Cob 7.8 pF at 0.1 V to 2.1 pF at 20 V; Cib 69 pF to 37 pF (typical curves)     [T]
*   fT peak 115 MHz at 10 mA (typical curve)                                       [T]
*   Not on datasheet: Rb, BR, storage time -> SPICE defaults                        [D]
* =====================================================================
.subckt MMBTA42 C B E
Q1 C B E Q_MMBTA42
.model Q_MMBTA42 NPN(Is=3.45e-14 Nf=1 Bf=155 Vaf=100 Ikf=0.035 Rc=0.8 Cje=71.6p Vje=0.877 Mje=0.347 Cjc=8.5p Vjc=0.307 Mjc=0.323 Tf=1.2n)
.ends MMBTA42

* =====================================================================
* Q1, Q7  MMBT3906 (PNP), MDD, LCSC C364311 (Rev 2024A2)
*   hFE about 180 at 0.1-3 mA, 112 at 30 mA, 50 at 100 mA (typical curve, VCE -1 V) [T]
*   VBE 0.664 V at 1 mA, VCE -1 V (typical IC-VBE curve)                           [T]
*   Early voltage about 100 V from the typical static characteristic              [T]
*   VCE(sat) 72 mV at 10 mA, 280 mV at 100 mA, beta 10 -> Rc 2.3 ohm               [T]
*   Cib 7.5 pF at 0.1 V to 3.6 pF at 5 V; Cob 8 pF to 2.3 pF at 20 V (typical)     [T]
*   fT peak 500 MHz at 10 mA (typical curve)                                       [T]
*   Storage time 225 ns max (IC 10 mA, IB1=IB2 1 mA) -> Tr 350 ns                   [M]
*   Not on datasheet: Rb, BR -> SPICE defaults                                     [D]
* =====================================================================
.subckt MMBT3906 C B E
Q1 C B E Q_MMBT3906
.model Q_MMBT3906 PNP(Is=6.9e-15 Nf=1 Bf=180 Vaf=100 Ikf=0.03 Rc=2.3 Cje=7.8p Vje=4.0 Mje=0.95 Cjc=8.4p Vjc=1.785 Mjc=0.524 Tf=0.27n Tr=350n)
.ends MMBT3906

* =====================================================================
* Q6  MMBT3904 (NPN), JSMSEMI, LCSC C916374
*   hFE about 130 flat 0.1-10 mA, 68 at 100 mA, 25 at 200 mA (Fig.3 typical, VCE 1 V) [T]
*   No IC-VBE curve: Is set from Fig.5 typical VBE(sat) 0.80 V at 10 mA, beta 10     [T]
*   VCE(sat) 80 mV at 10 mA, 300 mV at 200 mA (Fig.4 typical) -> Rc 1.1 ohm          [T]
*   Cibo 8 pF at 0.1 V to 4 pF at 5 V; Cobo 10.9 pF to 2.1 pF at 20 V (Fig.2)        [T]
*   fT 300 MHz min, no typical -> Tf 0.53 ns                                        [M]
*   Storage time 200 ns max (IC 10 mA, IB1=IB2 1 mA) -> Tr 320 ns                    [M]
*   Not on datasheet: Early voltage, Rb, BR -> SPICE defaults                        [D]
* =====================================================================
.subckt MMBT3904 C B E
Q1 C B E Q_MMBT3904
.model Q_MMBT3904 NPN(Is=3.7e-16 Nf=1 Bf=130 Ikf=0.06 Rc=1.1 Cje=8.4p Vje=0.676 Mje=0.346 Cjc=12.2p Vjc=0.445 Mjc=0.471 Tf=0.53n Tr=320n)
.ends MMBT3904

* =====================================================================
* U3, U5, U7  TCMT1108, Vishay, LCSC C3014154 (TCMT110. series, doc 83510 rev 3.1)
* Ports A K E C = symbol pins 1 2 3 4.
*   LED: Fig.5 typical 25 C, fitted 0.1-50 mA (error within 0.5 %); VF 1.35 V typ at 50 mA; Cj 8 pF typ [T]
*   CTR: 130-260 % at IF 5 mA, VCE 5 V, no typical -> midpoint 195 % (your choice)  [M]
*        scaled with IF by Fig.12 typical normalized CTR at 25 C:
*        0.13 @0.1 mA, 0.25 @0.2, 0.38 @0.5, 0.54 @1, 0.73 @2, 1.00 @5, 1.10 @10, 1.13 @20, 1.00 @40 mA [T]
*   Output stage: photocurrent drives the base of a transistor, so saturation and speed
*   depend on the collector current and load like the real part. Speed fitted to Fig.14
*   typical phase (-45 deg at about 310 kHz with RL 100 ohm, 56 kHz with RL 1 kohm).   [T]
*   The internal transistor gain (100) is not on the datasheet; only CTR x speed matter. [D]
*   Coupling capacitance 0.3 pF typ, dark current ignored (100 nA max).            [T]
* =====================================================================
.subckt TCMT1108 A K E C params: CTR5=1.95
Dled A M D_TCMT_LED
Vs M K 0
Ck A C 0.3p
* LED current copied onto node NI (1 V per A); base photocurrent = CTR5 x [IF x normalized CTR(IF)] / internal gain,
* tabulated as IF x NCTR(IF) so the function is continuous through zero current
Fcp 0 NI Vs 1
Rni NI 0 1
Bph 0 PB I = CTR5 / 100 * pwl(V(NI), -1,0, 0,0, 1e-4,1.3e-5, 2e-4,5e-5, 5e-4,1.9e-4, 1e-3,5.4e-4, 2e-3,1.46e-3, 5e-3,5e-3, 1e-2,1.1e-2, 2e-2,2.26e-2, 4e-2,4e-2)
Vpb PB B 0
Rpb B E 100Meg
Q1 C B E Q_TCMT_PT
.model D_TCMT_LED D(Is=1.01e-15 N=1.646 Rs=0.173 Cjo=8p)
.model Q_TCMT_PT NPN(Is=1e-14 Bf=100 Br=1 Cjc=36p Vjc=0.75 Mjc=0.33 Cje=10p Tf=3.2n)
.ends TCMT1108

* =====================================================================
* T1, T2  Coilcraft DA2034-AL (DA203x datasheet)
* Pin order matches the symbol power_supply:DA2034-ALD.
*   Primary inductance 10.0 uH +/-10 % at 0 A, primaries in parallel              [T]
*   (9.0 uH min at the 10 A peak: saturation NOT modelled)                         [M]
*   Turns ratio 1:10 -> secondary 1.0 mH                                           [T]
*   DCR 0.018 ohm primary (parallel), 1.75 ohm secondary: max only                 [M]
*   Leakage 0.250 uH max (primaries parallel, secondary shorted) -> k = 0.98742      [M]
*   Interwinding capacitance 128 pF (all primary to all secondary), split equally
*   between the dotted ends and the undotted ends                                  [T]
*   Not on datasheet: core loss, winding self-capacitance -> not modelled           [D]
*   Dots: primary start (P*S) and SDOT.
* =====================================================================
.subckt DA2034_AL SDOT NC1 P4F P3F P2F P1F P1S P2S P3S P4S NC2 S
Rpri P1S PI 0.018
Lpri PI P1F 10u
Lsec SDOT SI 1m
Rsec SI S 1.75
Kps Lpri Lsec 0.98742
Cdot P1S SDOT 64p
Cend P1F S 64p
Rt2s P2S P1S 1u
Rt3s P3S P1S 1u
Rt4s P4S P1S 1u
Rt2f P2F P1F 1u
Rt3f P3F P1F 1u
Rt4f P4F P1F 1u
Rnc1 NC1 SDOT 1G
Rnc2 NC2 SDOT 1G
.ends DA2034_AL

* =====================================================================
* FB1-FB3  Murata BLM31PG601SN1L, LCSC C16902 (spec JENF243A-0006V-01)
*   DC resistance 0.08 ohm typ (0.16 max)                                          [T]
*   Impedance 600 ohm +/-25 % at 100 MHz (typical)                                 [T]
*   No impedance-vs-frequency curve in this document: modelled as an inductor in
*   parallel with a resistor giving 600 ohm at 100 MHz with equal parts
*   (849 ohm, 1.35 uH). The split is an assumption; Murata's SPICE model would replace it. [D]
* =====================================================================
.subckt BLM31PG601SN1 P N
Rdc P X 0.08
Lb X N 1.35u
Rb X N 849
.ends BLM31PG601SN1

* =====================================================================
* Battery (simulation-only source on J1): typical 3S Li-ion pack
*   11.1 V open-circuit (3 x 3.7 V nominal), 0.15 ohm internal resistance
*   (no cell chosen yet: typical 18650 value, assumption)                           [D]
* =====================================================================
.subckt BATTERY_3S NEG POS params: VOC=11.1 RINT=0.15
Vb VB NEG {VOC}
Rb VB POS {RINT}
.ends BATTERY_3S
